|************************************************************************
| DATASHEET-DERIVED IBIS — NOT A VENDOR FILE.
|
| 74HC-family CMOS I/O at the VCC = 5.0 V operating point, hand-derived
| by the bhdl stdlib data campaign from PUBLISHED specification points:
|
|   * TI SN74HC08 datasheet (SCLS081) / SN74HC00 (SCLS047). The
|     datasheet publishes TWO characterization columns (VCC = 4.5 V,
|     rated IOL 4 mA; VCC = 6 V, rated IOL 5.2 mA); the tables below
|     are INTERPOLATED to the VCC = 5.0 V operating point between
|     those two published columns (drive scale 4.4/4.0 = 1.10):
|       VOL 0.1 V typ at IOL = 4 mA (4.5 V col) -> 23 ohm slope at 5 V
|       VOL 0.26 V MAX at IOL = 4 mA -> 59 ohm min-corner slope
|         (the guaranteed-worst device)
|       VOH VCC-0.1 V typ at -4 mA   -> pullup mirrors pulldown
|       input capacitance 3.5 pF typ -> C_comp
|       transition time 8 ns typ / 15 ns max at CL = 50 pF -> [Ramp]
|         (20-80% swing = 0.6 x 5.0 V = 3.0 V; tt scales ~vcc^-0.5,
|          ~7.5 ns at 5 V)
|   * Saturation plateau (~28 mA typ at large Vout) from the 74HC family
|     typical output characteristics published in Nexperia's family
|     specifications (the classic HC output curve knee).
|   * max corner = typ scaled +40% (strong-process bound, stated
|     assumption — no published max-drive spec exists for this family).
|   * Clamp tables = standard CMOS protection-diode curve (0.7 V knee).
|
| Every simulation consuming this file inherits these provenance notes:
| the derivation is honest interpolation BETWEEN published points, never
| invention beyond them.
|************************************************************************
